      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)+2{t}^{2}-t+1 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t)+{t}^{2}+4t-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe systems of linear ODEs above can be written in matrix form as follows:\n\n| ${x}^{′}(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,x(t)+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-3}} |  |  | $\\,\\,{t}^{2}\\,\\,+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-4}} |  |  | $\\,\\,t+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-5}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-6}} | {{field-7}} |  |  | {{field-8}} |  |  | {{field-9}} |  |  | {{field-10}} |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's rewrite our system, highlighting the coefficients:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=(-1)\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+3\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+2\\cdot {t}^{2}+(-1)\\cdot t+1 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+(-2)\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+1\\cdot {t}^{2}+4\\cdot t+(-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in matrix form:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{t}^{2}+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}].$",
